<BaseLayout title="About — Alexander Mervar" description="About Alexander Mervar — essays and film criticism.">
  <h1>About</h1>

  <figure class="about-photo">
    <img src="/images/about.jpg" alt="Alexander Mervar, outdoors on a sunny day" />
  </figure>

  <p>I'm Alexander. I write essays and film criticism, and this site is where I publish it — on my own terms, in one place.</p>

  <p>Writing is how I figure out what I actually think. I'm drawn to film, history, and psychology — not as separate beats but as different ways into the same question: why people do what they do, and how they make sense of their own moment. A review of a film and a piece about the past are, to me, the same kind of work.</p>

  <p>That instinct comes partly from studying <a href="https://cogs.indiana.edu" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Cognitive Science</a> at Indiana University — an odd, cross-disciplinary field pulling from psychology, neuroscience, computer science, linguistics, and philosophy, all aimed at understanding how minds work. It gave me a way of looking at human behavior that takes both the messy and the formal seriously, and it still shapes how I read a film or a story.</p>

  <p>The goal here is simple and a little old-fashioned: make work worth paying attention to, and build a real readership around it — the kind of small, direct relationship between a writer and the people who actually want to read them. If that's you, the best way to follow along is to <a href="/subscribe">subscribe</a>.</p>

  <h2>The other things I do</h2>

  <p>Writing isn't the whole picture. By day I work as a Workday consultant in technology consulting — genuinely interesting problems about systems and the people who use them, and a place I keep learning. I also tinker with code: I built <a href="https://github.com/alexandermervar/agent-manager" target="_blank" rel="noopener">agent-manager</a>, a small open-source tool for running AI agents, and I run a Raspberry Pi homelab (HAL-1000) that hosts, among other things, a bot that posts my film watches to Mastodon. Different surfaces, same underlying habit: understanding systems and the humans inside them.</p>

  <h2>Find me elsewhere</h2>

  <p>I log films on <a href="https://letterboxd.com/macDoofOS/" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">Letterboxd</a> and turn up on <a href="https://hachyderm.io/@macDoofOS" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">Mastodon</a>.</p>

  <h2>Get in touch</h2>

  <p>Email is best — <span class="email-display">hello&#32;&#91;at&#93;&#32;alexandermervar&#32;&#91;dot&#93;&#32;com</span> — or find me on <a href="https://hachyderm.io/@macDoofOS" rel="me noopener" target="_blank">Mastodon</a>.</p>
